cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  praxis — a legal assistant for Russian law whose citations are checked
message: >-
  If you use praxis in work you publish, please cite it using this entry.
abstract: >-
  A question-answering system over Russian statutory law. Retrieval is hybrid -- lexical plus dense with a cross-encoder reranker -- and a natural language inference model checks that each cited provision supports the claim it is attached to, so an unsupported citation is caught rather than returned. The default answer is extractive.
authors:
  - family-names: Drobyshev
    given-names: Denis
repository-code: https://github.com/DrobyshevDev/praxis
url: https://github.com/DrobyshevDev/praxis
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - legal-tech
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - citation-verification
  - natural-language-inference
  - russian
  - information-retrieval
